<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Castiglione delle Stiviere</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Castiglione delle Stiviere is a town in the province of Mantua in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-garda">Lake Garda</a>. It was ruled by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga family</a> as a marquisate and principality, and was the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aloysius-gonzaga">Saint Aloysius</a> Gonzaga. In 1796 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> defeated the Austrians nearby, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-solferino">Battle of Solferino</a> in 1859 Henri Dunant cared for the wounded in the town, an experience that led to the founding of the Red Cross.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/castiglione-delle-stiviere.jpg" alt="Castiglione delle Stiviere" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Massimo Telò · CC BY 2.5 it · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castiglione_delle_Stiviere_(panorama).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
